{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
  "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:11 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what -- what about Clemons? Because Clemons is a precedent of this Court that says that the appellate court can do reweighing. Is that still good law?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Blackmun",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0000-0003",
      "kind": "dissent",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There was a passionate dissent, you've read it, by Justice Blackmun saying this"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: I -- I couldn't disagree more profoundly with that. That is, that what we're not seeking here is not formalistic; what we're saying is that there is new state action as a result of the Ninth Circuit's decision."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: At the risk of a formalistic question, normally, states are the definers of their own procedures, their own"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: So there's no difference between sort of a surgical mistake that could be corrected and an entirely comprehensive mistake that infects the whole proceeding?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SKINNER: The Court certainly is in a position to dismiss the case as improvidently granted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Here, Petitioner challenged the existing aggravators, and the court said we're not going there."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF NEAL K. KATYAL ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, Justice Kavanaugh, you asked me about Justice Blackmun's dissent, which I had an occasion to look at again just now."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "They considered, for example, the aggravators and weighed them, at Petition Appendix pages 4a and 7a."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1109",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "e93fa9e20780322b453431c24f93cedcfa08f102032aefc8319118b092edec17",
      "evidence_id": "ev-e93fa9e20780-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted. (Whereupon, 12:11 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
